<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">UNESCO</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1945–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">UNESCO, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization, is a specialised agency of the United Nations founded in 1945 and based in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>. It promotes international cooperation in education, science, culture and communication. Through the World Heritage Convention of 1972 it keeps the World Heritage List of cultural and natural sites of outstanding universal value, and it also records the intangible cultural heritage of humanity.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/unesco.jpg" alt="UNESCO" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mouagip · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_UNESCO.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
